# Using International Gold Price XAU in Google Sheets

We're using a 3rt-party price provider, Gold API, for this example.  
**Please note** that I'm not affiliated with the company in any shape or form. Please use their service using your own discretion.
Also, they have a monthly, free quota of 100 API hits only, so this won't be very useful for any serious application. This will fit personal finance, hobby projects etc.

## 1. Create an account to get your API-key, YOUR_API_KEY.
It will look like `goldapi-u6i1randomcharso5l9k3-io`. This is what you need 

## 2. Access Google Apps Script

Open your Google Sheet where you are going to use the gold-price.
In the menu bar, go to `Extensions > Apps Script`. This will open a new browser tab with the `script editor`.

In the script editor, you will see a file named `Code.gs` with a default function. 
Replace all the existing code with the following script.

```
function GOLD_API_XAUUSD() {

  url = "https://www.goldapi.io/api/XAU/USD";
  headers = {
    'x-access-token': 'INSERT_YOUR_OWN_KEY'
  };

  const response = UrlFetchApp.fetch(url, { method: 'GET', muteHttpExceptions: true, headers: headers });
  const json = JSON.parse(response.getContentText());

  // console.info(json);
  price_xau = json['price']; // uncomment this to get XAU:USD price
  price_gram_usd = json['price_gram_24k'];
  // console.info(price_xau, price_gram_usd);  // uncomment this to get XAU:USD price
  return price_gram_usd;  // // uncomment this to get XAU:USD per gram price
}
```

Save the script.

3. Now, go back to the Google Sheet, and you should be able to use `GOLD_API_XAUUSD()` function anywhere in the Sheet.
